-- int-grant.l4: integration points IP5, IP6, IP11, IP17 and headline (a): may this person be granted this licence on this day.
-- The INTEGRATOR's module.  Group 2 decides the Registrar's duty to grant (s.6(a)) and the Second Schedule route; four of its inputs
-- belong to other groups and are supplied here:
--   IP5   "the programme was approved by the Registrar" and "the foreign qualification was recognised": group 4 (s.19(b), s.19(c)),
--         the Council's advice (IP7) being worked out by group 4 from a consultation record;
--   IP11  "the fee was paid in full": group 8's regulation 4, which bars the Registrar from giving or renewing a licence for which a fee
--         was fixed and not paid in full (the fee is the vintage's, updated by regulation 3 from the first 1 January);
--   IP2   "the commencement day": group 7's day (s.63(a)(1)), through int-commencement, for the three-year note of the Second Schedule;
--   IP6   the training required: group 2's items for the application, returned unchanged for a caller to read.
-- What is decided here that no group decided.
--   COMMENCEMENT OF THE REGISTRAR'S DUTY.  s.63(a) fixes a commencement only "for the performance of work on a system"; it says nothing
--   of the Registrar's duty to grant (group 7, fork F-C-7, trap T20).  Group 2 states no gate.  The headline therefore answers only
--   for an application made on or after the commencement day of s.63(a)(1), the first day on which any reading gives the Registrar a
--   live duty, and returns a named refusal before it: the sources do not say whether the Registrar's duty ran earlier.  The ungated
--   group 2 function is `the Registrar must grant the licence` itself (callable; the alternative reading).
--   "APPROVED" MEANS CONSENT TO THE PROGRAMME.  Group 4 has two functions for s.19(b): the programme HAS the Registrar's consent, and
--   it SATISFIES THE REQUIREMENT of consent (true also for a programme that needs none).  The headline takes the first, the stricter:
--   a programme that cannot yield a final certificate cannot be the programme of s.6(a)(4)(a) in any case.  The other is callable.

§ `Integration points IP5, IP6, IP11, IP17 and headline (a): the grant of a licence`

§§ `The facts of an application`

@ref Law s.19(c)(1), s.19(c)(2), s.24 to 26 (IP5, IP7)
@desc A foreign certificate, degree or training the applicant relies on, what the Registrar considered, and the consultation of the Council that s.19(c) requires
DECLARE `Foreign qualification relied on` HAS
    `the foreign qualification` IS A `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` @desc The qualification and the Registrar's opinion and decision about it
    `what the Registrar considered` IS A `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)` @desc The four matters the Registrar must weigh
    `the consultation of the Council` IS A `Consultation of the Council` @desc The consultation of the Council before the recognition: its function, whether it was requested and the source of the advice

@ref Law s.6(a), s.19(b), s.19(c), regulation 4 of the Fees Regulations (IP5, IP11, IP17)
@desc Everything the Registrar's duty to grant a licence under s.6(a) asks that is not on the Application itself: the Registrar's opinion on fitness, whether the training the Second Schedule requires was completed, the programme and the foreign qualification relied on, and the fee paid under the vintage of the Fees Regulations
DECLARE `Facts of a grant under section 6` HAS
    `the application` IS AN Application @desc The applicant, what they hold, the kind of licence sought and the day of the application
    `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Registrar's opinion (s.6(a)(3)), an input
    `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the applicant completed what column B of the Second Schedule requires for the route they take
    `the programme the applicant completed` IS A MAYBE `Study programme under section 19(b)` @desc The programme in which the training was completed; NOTHING if there is none (then no programme was approved)
    `the foreign qualification relied on` IS A MAYBE `Foreign qualification relied on` @desc A foreign qualification relied on in place of the training; NOTHING if none
    `the vintage of the Fees Regulations` IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations` @desc The text of the Fees Regulations that governs the fee
    `the amount paid for the licence` IS A NUMBER @desc What the applicant paid, in new shekels
    `the index readings` IS A LIST OF `Price index reading` @desc The consumer price index readings with their publication days (regulation 3 updates the fee from the first 1 January; the sources contain none)

@ref Law s.19(b) (IP5)
@desc True if the programme the applicant completed had the Registrar's consent; false where there is no such programme
GIVEN f IS A `Facts of a grant under section 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the Registrar approved the programme in` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `the programme the applicant completed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST programme THEN `s 19(b) — the study programme has the Registrar's consent` programme

@ref Law s.19(b) (IP5), the alternative
@desc The same, reading a programme that needs no consent as satisfying the requirement (group 4's other function)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts of a grant under section 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int (a programme that needs no consent satisfies the requirement) — the requirement of the Registrar's consent is met by the programme in` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `the programme the applicant completed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST programme THEN `s 19(b) — the study programme satisfies the requirement of the Registrar's consent` programme

@ref Law s.19(c) with s.24 to 26 (IP5, IP7)
@desc True if a foreign qualification was recognised in accordance with s.19(c): the Registrar recognised it, was entitled to (the Council consulted and its advice validly given), considered the four matters, and any condition was met; false where none is relied on
GIVEN f IS A `Facts of a grant under section 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the foreign qualification was recognised in` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `the foreign qualification relied on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST q THEN `s 19(c) with ss 24 to 26 — the foreign qualification was recognised:` (q's `the foreign qualification`) `having considered` (q's `what the Registrar considered`) `after the consultation` (q's `the consultation of the Council`)

@ref Fees Regulations regulation 2(c), regulation 3, regulation 4 (IP11)
@desc True if regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give the licence: the fee fixed for receiving a licence in the vintage, updated to the day of the application, was paid in full, or none is fixed
GIVEN f IS A `Facts of a grant under section 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the fee for the licence was paid in full in` f MEANS
    `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage`
        (f's `the vintage of the Fees Regulations`)
        `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal`
        (f's `the amount paid for the licence`)
        (f's `the application`'s `the day of the application`)
        (f's `the index readings`)

§§ `Headline (a): may this person be granted this licence on this day`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`int — the sources do not say whether the Registrar's duty to grant ran before the commencement day of section 63(a)(1)` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Law fixes a commencement only for work on a system (s.63(a)); it does not say when the Registrar's duty to grant (s.6) begins, and the day is before the commencement day of s.63(a)(1)"

@ref Law s.6(a), s.19(b), s.19(c), s.24 to 26, s.63(a), Second Schedule, regulations 2(c), 3, 4 of the Fees Regulations
@export Whether the Registrar must grant the licence sought: the conditions of s.6(a)(1) to (4) all hold (full age, citizen or resident, no disqualifying offence in the Registrar's opinion, one of the training routes of the Second Schedule completed in an approved programme or a foreign qualification recognised after the Council's valid advice), regulation 4 does not bar the Registrar (the fee fixed in the vintage, updated, was paid), and the application is made on or after the commencement day; a named refusal for an application made before it
GIVEN f IS A `Facts of a grant under section 6` @desc The application and the facts group 2 asks that are not on it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` f MEANS
    IF   f's `the application`'s `the day of the application` LESS THAN `int — the commencement day`
    THEN `int — the sources do not say whether the Registrar's duty to grant ran before the commencement day of section 63(a)(1)`
    ELSE `the Registrar must grant the licence`
             (f's `the application`)
             `int — the commencement day`
             (f's `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee`)
             (f's `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed`)
             (`int — the Registrar approved the programme in` f)
             (`int — the foreign qualification was recognised in` f)
             (`int — the fee for the licence was paid in full in` f)

@ref Law s.6(a), group 2 fork FC1 (the alternative)
@desc The same, with no commencement gate (group 2's own reading: ss.6 to 9 state none)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts of a grant under section 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int (with no commencement gate) — the Registrar must grant the licence on` f MEANS
    `the Registrar must grant the licence`
        (f's `the application`)
        `int — the commencement day`
        (f's `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee`)
        (f's `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed`)
        (`int — the Registrar approved the programme in` f)
        (`int — the foreign qualification was recognised in` f)
        (`int — the fee for the licence was paid in full in` f)

@ref Law s.6(a)(4), Second Schedule (IP6)
@export The items of the Second Schedule that apply to the application: the Part sought, the prior training and experience in column A, the training or certificate required in column B (hours being a ceiling), the three-year note counted from the commencement day of s.63(a)(1); a named refusal where the rows conflict on the reading taken
GIVEN application IS AN Application @desc The licence application: the applicant and what they hold, the kind of licence sought and the day of the application
GIVETH A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
`int — the training the Second Schedule requires for` application MEANS
    `training required for the licence sought` application `int — the commencement day`

@ref Law s.6(a)(4), Second Schedule (IP6; fork F-C-3 of group 7)
@desc The items of the Second Schedule that apply to the application, with the commencement day of s.63(a)(1) read as three months from the later of the two days (16.10.2025) instead of the later of the two dates (16.7.2025): only the three-year notes of items A2, B4 and C5 move
GIVEN application IS AN Application @desc The licence application: the applicant and what they hold, the kind of licence sought and the day of the application
GIVETH A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
`int (three months from the later of the two days) — the training the Second Schedule requires for` application MEANS
    `training required for the licence sought` application `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the commencement day`

@ref Law s.9, regulation 2(d) of the Fees Regulations (IP11, IP17)
@desc The facts of a foreign expert's application for a temporary licence beyond the application itself: the Registrar's recognition, the vintage and the fee paid
DECLARE `Facts of a grant of a temporary licence under section 9` HAS
    `the expert` IS A `Foreign expert's application under section 9` @desc The foreign expert's application and the facts s.9(a) asks of the applicant
    `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Registrar's recognition (s.9(a)(3)), an input
    `the vintage of the Fees Regulations` IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations` @desc The text of the Fees Regulations that governs the fee
    `the amount paid for the application` IS A NUMBER @desc What the expert paid, in new shekels
    `the index readings` IS A LIST OF `Price index reading` @desc The consumer price index readings (regulation 3); the sources contain none

@ref Law s.9(a), regulation 2(d), regulation 4 (IP11)
@export Whether the Registrar may grant a temporary grade 3 licence to the foreign expert: from a foreign state, invited to work on a system over 70 kW, authorised abroad and done similar work in the six preceding years, recognised by the Registrar, with the fee fixed for the application in the vintage (updated) paid in full; the application must be made on or after the commencement day, a named refusal before it
GIVEN g IS A `Facts of a grant of a temporary licence under section 9` @desc The expert's application, the Registrar's recognition and the fee paid
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the Registrar may grant a temporary licence on` g MEANS
    IF   g's `the expert`'s `the application`'s `the day of the application` LESS THAN `int — the commencement day`
    THEN `int — the sources do not say whether the Registrar's duty to grant ran before the commencement day of section 63(a)(1)`
    ELSE `the temporary licence may be granted`
             (g's `the expert`)
             (g's `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field`)
             (`regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage`
                  (g's `the vintage of the Fees Regulations`)
                  `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal`
                  (g's `the amount paid for the application`)
                  (g's `the expert`'s `the application`'s `the day of the application`)
                  (g's `the index readings`))

§§ `Renewal under section 8`

@ref Law s.8, s.6(a)(1) to (3), regulations 2(c), 3 and 4 of the Fees Regulations (IP11, IP17)
@desc The facts of an application to renew a licence beyond the application itself: the Registrar's opinion on fitness, the vintage and the fee paid
DECLARE `Facts of a renewal under section 8` HAS
    `the application` IS AN Application @desc The application to renew: the applicant, the kind sought, the day of the application
    `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Registrar's opinion (s.6(a)(3)), an input
    `the vintage of the Fees Regulations` IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations` @desc The text of the Fees Regulations that governs the fee
    `the amount paid for the renewal` IS A NUMBER @desc What the applicant paid, in new shekels
    `the index readings` IS A LIST OF `Price index reading` @desc The consumer price index readings (regulation 3); the sources contain none

@ref Law s.8, s.6(a)(1) to (3) (IP17)
@desc True if the conditions of s.6(a)(1) to (3) hold for the applicant to renew (the training of (4) is not asked again)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts of a renewal under section 8`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the conditions of section 8 hold for the renewal in` f MEANS
    `s 8 — the licence can be renewed for the applicant` (f's `the application`) (f's `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee`)

@ref regulation 2(c), 3 and 4 of the Fees Regulations (IP11)
@desc True if regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to renew: the fee fixed for receiving a licence or renewing it, updated to the day, was paid in full
GIVEN f IS A `Facts of a renewal under section 8`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the fee for the renewal was paid in full in` f MEANS
    `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` (f's `the vintage of the Fees Regulations`) `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` (f's `the amount paid for the renewal`) (f's `the application`'s `the day of the application`) (f's `the index readings`)

@ref Law s.8, s.6(a)(1) to (3), regulation 4 (IP11)
@export Whether a licence can be renewed on the application: the conditions of s.6(a)(1) to (3) hold (the training of (4) is not asked again, s.8), regulation 4 does not bar the Registrar (the fee for receiving a licence or renewing it, updated, was paid), and the application is made on or after the commencement day; a named refusal for an application made before it
GIVEN f IS A `Facts of a renewal under section 8` @desc The application to renew and the facts group 2 and group 8 ask beyond it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the licence can be renewed on` f MEANS
    IF   f's `the application`'s `the day of the application` LESS THAN `int — the commencement day`
    THEN `int — the sources do not say whether the Registrar's duty to grant ran before the commencement day of section 63(a)(1)`
    ELSE `int — the conditions of section 8 hold for the renewal in` f AND `int — the fee for the renewal was paid in full in` f
